<title>GAMBIA: New Islamic bank licensed in Gambia.</title>
<headline>New Islamic bank licensed in Gambia.</headline>
<dateline>BANJUL 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Gambia Islamic Bank has been granted a licence to operate as a commercial bank, the country's central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It would operate under Islamic law, which prohibits the charging of interest and can offer loans of up to $2 million to small and medium-scale industries. It's funds are expected to come from the Saudi-based Islamic Development Bank.</p>
<p>The new bank opens for business in the first week of October, banking sources said.</p>
</text>
